{
  "requirement": "The `Yaml` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct Yaml;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Yaml;\nimpl Debug for Yaml;\nimpl Default for Yaml;\nimpl OutlineLang for Yaml;\nimpl Copy for Yaml;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.sources.yaml.Yaml` has two obligations. One is the declaration: `pub struct Yaml;` with `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `OutlineLang` and `Copy` implementations. The other is that the `OutlineLang` implementation supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules described in the chapter.\n\n**Declaration and trait implementations**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` compares each declaration's trait-implementation set against rustdoc's. It does this through `check_declaration`, which asserts `Trait implementations for {id}`. A missing or extra impl, including `Debug`, would fail it. It also checks the declaration and member names.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` calls the nested `check` helper with `languages::Yaml`. The helper's `L: OutlineLang + Default + Copy` bound compiles only if those impls exist. It calls `Clone::clone` and `L::default()`. It asserts `size_of::<L>() == 0`, which fits a unit struct.\n\n**`OutlineLang` behavior for YAML**\n- The `check` helper asserts the extensions `[\"yml\", \"yaml\"]` and the fingerprint scheme `yaml-structural-v1`. It uses a filename of `a.YAML`, and it also tries each extension in uppercase.\n- It asserts that outlines built by inference and by explicit language are consistent. The root item has selector `\"\"` and covers the whole source. `pair[check]` selects, and the fingerprints match.\n- It also checks that `search_structure` returns valid ranges.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[yaml_selection_includes_comments_owned_by_the_entry]` asserts YAML selection. It covers a trailing comment, a preceding comment owned by the next pair, nested pairs and item spans.\n\n**Delegated obligations:** the detailed extension, selection and fingerprint rules belong to the refining requirements `requirements.sdk.sources.yaml.language`, `requirements.sdk.sources.yaml.items` and `requirements.sdk.sources.yaml.fingerprints`. I did not reassess them here.\n\nI found no gap.",
  "references": "938ac8df4e2c00b158fa9033d713e6ed4571a3207a735a8defa9584e148cc342",
